  - question: "What is PHP2Shell?"
    answer: "PHP2Shell is the name for two critical PHP vulnerabilities published on October 21, 2026, [CVE-2026-109618](https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w) and [CVE-2026-109619](https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp). Both score 9.2 on CVSS v4 and let an unauthenticated attacker run code on PHP served through web SAPIs such as Apache mod_php and PHP-FPM. PHP 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36, and 8.2.35 fix them."
